From ca0059a16760f8e0308d2537708b054a8868ca27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:52:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] Add a multiboot flasher that writes the repro link
 program into the cart

The flasher runs on the GBA (sent with a GameCube link cable ROM sender)
with the repro Emerald cart inserted, and rewrites Emerald's built-in
Colosseum link program in the cart's ROM flash. make_flasher.py builds it
from the user's own dump and the BPS patch; the code carries no ROM data.

Before writing, it checks the cart against the dump, probes the board with
the save code's probe, reads the erase block size from CFI and verifies it
by test-erasing in an area that is empty in the dump. Each block is copied
with the new bytes to a spare empty block and checked before the game
block is erased and rewritten from it, so a rerun after a power cut
finishes the job. Flash commands and SRAM banking are the save code's.

sim_cart gains CFI geometry, a switch to make CFI misreport the block
size, and power cycles that leave an interrupted erase half done.
flasher_emu_test.py runs the built flasher against every simulated board
with power cuts, failed operations, wrong CFI tables and refusals.

Also stop tracking Python bytecode caches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014JPQshc9oBXnzvR2E67Khm
